{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/943754-police-in-wod","id":943754,"title":"Police in WoD","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-04T11:58:21-07:00","id":943754,"title":"Police in WoD","content":"I am just sort of curious how STs portray police in their games? In a lot of my games, the police end up being the allies of the PCs, though there is the occasional 'bad cop' that is corrupt and willingly works for the enemy. I find it easy for Werewolves to make friends with the local police and, in the case of rural cops, many of their Kinfolk end up being the law in the rural communities where they prefer to live. In the case of Vampires, it takes a little more effort, but injecting small amounts of blood in the doughnuts that they give to the cops for free will often make the cops friendly (the idea is to balance the level of the blood bond at level two without allowing it to fall to level one or rise to level three).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T12:01:57-07:00","id":943758,"title":"","content":"I pretty much run them like normal police, some are bad, some are just in for a paycheck and a fat pension but most are genuinely good people who suffer the misfortune of having to deal with humanity at its worse on a regular basis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T14:51:34-07:00","id":943903,"title":"","content":"I imagine a lot of Cops discover the truth about the supernatural<br /> <br /> Sadly the bravest amongst them, those who do what is morally right, also have an excellent chance of dieing in short order<br /> <br /> Would seem a valid background for a Hunter I think<br /> <br /> Either working on his own or maybe being recruited by SAD<br /> <br /> SAD is on the lookout for cops in the know, both for debriefing and possible recruitment.<br /> <br /> the cowardly (or simply practical) do absolutely nothing about it)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> And of course some are Kinfolk or even Garou Struggling to balance a life in uniform with the difficultys of sept life.<br /> <br /> using their gifts (or connections with the sept) to solve some crimes that otherwise would be unsolvable<br /> <br /> and to ensure that other crimes, for the greater good, are never solved to protect the veil<br /> <br /> As well likely as some formori both those that are, and that are not, affiliated with Pentex.<br /> <br /> As well as ghouls or maybe enchanted, who are both used by their masters as contacts.<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> <br /> Oh a closely related issue? CPS?<br /> <br /> First look at what Real CPS is capable of without evil spirits, Vampires, or Formori manipulating them...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://medicalkidnap.com/2015/07/21/child-sex-trafficking-through-child-protection-services-exposed-kidnapping-children-for-sex/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"http://medicalkidnap.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2020/12/BitChute.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://medicalkidnap.com/2015/07/21/child-sex-trafficking-through-child-protection-services-exposed-kidnapping-children-for-sex/\" target=\"_blank\"> &ndash; Page not found </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://medicalkidnap.com/2015/07/21/child-sex-trafficking-through-child-protection-services-exposed-kidnapping-children-for-sex/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://medicalkidnap.com/2015/07/21/child-sex-trafficking-through-child-protection-services-exposed-kidnapping-children-for-sex/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Shudder to think what they'd think of WITH all those things.<br /> <br /> ideas of how to use the CPS as a foil that is effective but not unstoppable most likely in either changeling or Werewolf<br /> <br /> parents in either group could come across as &quot;eccentric&quot; at best and &quot;nutty&quot; at worse. thus prompting a visit from them<br /> <br /> Garou would either have to shred them then disappear themselves and their children<br /> <br /> or to try using persuasion not sure of any other tricks garou have that would help<br /> <br /> Changelings have soveregn if they spend enough glamour to lower the difficulty enough they can make anything look like a good idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":". 08-04-2016, 07:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T20:54:25-07:00","id":944104,"title":"","content":"Being a darker version of our world my take on police is that overall they are more corrupt and dirty than in real life. But this varies from location and location and cop to cop. Some are still good people trying to do the best they can, lots are just there to get paid and retire early Nd others are willing to take money from anyone who offers. Most of the higher ups in major cities especially are controlled by someone/ something, either by bribes, blackmail, domination or some other means.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12161-browman","name":"Browman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T21:12:00-07:00","id":944110,"title":"","content":"I think that they are also controlled by elected officials, who are beholden to monied interests, like vampires, or who are Infernalists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T00:00:29-07:00","id":944162,"title":"","content":"Totally controlled by the local Vampires. Most cops get dominated, blood bound, Presenced, and /or Blackmailed into looking away from Vampire Activities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11217-kurseteller","name":"kurseteller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11217_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T08:17:19-07:00","id":944327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kurseteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/943754-police-in-wod?p=944162#post944162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Totally controlled by the local Vampires. Most cops get dominated, blood bound, Presenced, and /or Blackmailed into looking away from Vampire Activities.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I think their more passively redirected, then &quot;Totally controlled&quot; </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The vamps only control who they need to, and hunters from the Police do emerge Im sure.</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T09:31:32-07:00","id":944369,"title":"","content":"Vamps,demons, mages, werewolves and even organised crime all have their fingers in the police somewhere.<br /> It's world of darkness. They're corrupt, and a good portion of the guys going into the police to do genuine good get it beat out of them or they go missing. Now, some of the police are the genuine real deal who're out to help people, and it's been established that the good cops can occasionally give out some decent info, because it's not like the vampires can get to everyone in a metropolitan police force.<br /> <br /> 5% Outspokenly good guys, who will likely die.<br /> 15% genuinely good guys trying to do their best for the world, but probably try to keep their heads down.<br /> 40% Not exactly a model officer. Hits captives, doesn't care for victims, would take a good bribe every now and then. Would probably be the perpetrator of a controversial shooting. Mostly 'Does his job' <br /> 30% Take bribes consistently, hide evidence, arrange accidents<br /> 10% genuine fucking psychos<br /> <br /> Also, More police have guns. This is even in countries where the police don't normally have guns.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7244,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7244-innocent-flower","user":"Innocent Flower","date":". 08-05-2016, 12:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7244-innocent-flower","name":"Innocent Flower","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7244_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T10:57:54-07:00","id":944414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/943754-police-in-wod#post943754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am just sort of curious how STs portray police in their games? In a lot of my games, the police end up being the allies of the PCs, though there is the occasional 'bad cop' that is corrupt and willingly works for the enemy. I find it easy for Werewolves to make friends with the local police and, in the case of rural cops, many of their Kinfolk end up being the law in the rural communities where they prefer to live. In the case of Vampires, it takes a little more effort, but injecting small amounts of blood in the doughnuts that they give to the cops for free will often make the cops friendly (the idea is to balance the level of the blood bond at level two without allowing it to fall to level one or rise to level three).</div> </div> </div> </div>Cool description.<br /> <br /> For a short description of the police in my games, I go with, &quot;Slightly more incompetent and corrupt than the ones in Gotham City.&quot; If the police arrive at a situation involving the supernatural they're likely to cut and run but if they do stay, then they're likely to random shoot at everything and make up whatever story they can. The police are almost always under the control of vampires in the WoD but they're unaware of the truth--instead believing they're taking bribes from the uber-rich and mafia of the city. In my WOD, every police station has a room for working over suspects, isolating criminals until they confess to whatever is done, and evidence lockers where cash as well as drugs routinely disappear.<br /> <br /> It's not at all how I feel about the police in RL save perhaps the worst places in America but it fits my view of the WoD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T11:08:48-07:00","id":944418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/943754-police-in-wod?p=944414#post944414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Cool description.<br /> <br /> For a short description of the police in my games, I go with, &quot;Slightly more incompetent and corrupt than the ones in Gotham City.&quot; If the police arrive at a situation involving the supernatural they're likely to cut and run but if they do stay, then they're likely to random shoot at everything and make up whatever story they can. The police are almost always under the control of vampires in the WoD but they're unaware of the truth--instead believing they're taking bribes from the uber-rich and mafia of the city. In my WOD, every police station has a room for working over suspects, isolating criminals until they confess to whatever is done, and evidence lockers where cash as well as drugs routinely disappear.<br /> <br /> It's not at all how I feel about the police in RL save perhaps the worst places in America but it fits my view of the WoD.</div> </div> </div> </div>I usually do it this way for cities, with more rural police stations being a bit better about it.<br /> <br /> Garou don't/can't have good relations with police due to the Curse. And there is no guarantee of Kinfolk being police outside of a mostly exclusive kinfolk town.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T11:10:23-07:00","id":944420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/943754-police-in-wod?p=944418#post944418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I usually do it this way for cities, with more rural police stations being a bit better about it.<br /> <br /> Garou don't/can't have good relations with police due to the Curse. And there is no guarantee of Kinfolk being police outside of a mostly exclusive kinfolk town.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, Kinfolk being police isn't always a good thing for anyone but werewolves.<br /> <br /> As I explained in my game, Samuel Haight was Children of Gaia Kinfolk.<br /> <br /> Even the nice and fuzzy ones are still pretty terrifying to normal people.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T11:40:00-07:00","id":944429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/943754-police-in-wod?p=944420#post944420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also, Kinfolk being police isn't always a good thing for anyone but werewolves.<br /> <br /> As I explained in my game, Samuel Haight was Children of Gaia Kinfolk.<br /> <br /> Even the nice and fuzzy ones are still pretty terrifying to normal people.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. And it's worth remembering that the Curse does affect Kinfolk.<br /> So it has come up in a game I was in where a Garou PC confronted a Kinfolk cop and ended up getting shot for &quot;threatening an officer&quot; even though he was trying to help.<br /> <br /> I can only imagine the sort of trouble a Garou cop would run into. That should be a job most Garou could hold for very long at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T11:53:55-07:00","id":944438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Browman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/943754-police-in-wod?p=944104#post944104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Being a darker version of our world my take on police is that overall they are more corrupt and dirty than in real life. But this varies from location and location and cop to cop. Some are still good people trying to do the best they can, lots are just there to get paid and retire early Nd others are willing to take money from anyone who offers. Most of the higher ups in major cities especially are controlled by someone/ something, either by bribes, blackmail, domination or some other means.</div> </div> </div> </div>For most every campaign i have ran, i have usually had at LEAST one of the main power brokers, controlling the cops in some way, heck in some cities its a contested control (like ventrue vs glass walkers).. The every day beat cop on the street might not know WHO'S pulling the strings, but they may work out that someone is doing so..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/943754-police-in-wod?p=944110#post944110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that they are also controlled by elected officials, who are beholden to monied interests, like vampires, or who are Infernalists.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not just that, but often sheriffs and such are voted for, especially out in the boonies from the local population. So there exists a likelyhood some super has his tendrils in the sheriff..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Innocent Flower</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/943754-police-in-wod?p=944369#post944369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vamps,demons, mages, werewolves and even organised crime all have their fingers in the police somewhere.<br /> It's world of darkness. They're corrupt, and a good portion of the guys going into the police to do genuine good get it beat out of them or they go missing. Now, some of the police are the genuine real deal who're out to help people, and it's been established that the good cops can occasionally give out some decent info, because it's not like the vampires can get to everyone in a metropolitan police force.<br /> <br /> 5% Outspokenly good guys, who will likely die.<br /> 15% genuinely good guys trying to do their best for the world, but probably try to keep their heads down.<br /> 40% Not exactly a model officer. Hits captives, doesn't care for victims, would take a good bribe every now and then. Would probably be the perpetrator of a controversial shooting. Mostly 'Does his job'<br /> 30% Take bribes consistently, hide evidence, arrange accidents<br /> 10% genuine fucking psychos<br /> <br /> Also, More police have guns. This is even in countries where the police don't normally have guns.</div> </div> </div> </div>While you #s are good, i wuld say the 40% and 30% lines should be reversed..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T12:12:48-07:00","id":944453,"title":"","content":"There are places in the world where police kinfolks are pretty strategic. For example, the only road that connects two cities and goes through wilderness, the classic Lupine Alley. Guess who is the traffic cop? Yeah, the Kinfolk with a Gift of sniffing Wyrm. Everytime he stops a car, he reaches out to tell if there are vampires inside. If there are, he reports the description of the car and the direction where it went to the Garou.<br /> <br /> Same applies to railroads that fit the Lupine Alley description. But there not only police may be revealed to be kinfolk, the kinfolk conductor works equally as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12156-the-caitiff-antediluvian","name":"The Caitiff Antediluvian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T12:27:27-07:00","id":944460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Caitiff Antediluvian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/943754-police-in-wod?p=944453#post944453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are places in the world where police kinfolks are pretty strategic. For example, the only road that connects two cities and goes through wilderness, the classic Lupine Alley. Guess who is the traffic cop? Yeah, the Kinfolk with a Gift of sniffing Wyrm. Everytime he stops a car, he reaches out to tell if there are vampires inside. If there are, he reports the description of the car and the direction where it went to the Garou.<br /> <br /> Same applies to railroads that fit the Lupine Alley description. But there not only police may be revealed to be kinfolk, the kinfolk conductor works equally as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Kinfolk with Gifts are very rare. And that isn't really how Sense Wyrm works in any case. It would also go against tradition (which is a big thing for Garou) to have Kinfolk out sniffing around for the Wyrm. While I could see this used as a story point for a Vampire game (or even having a Garou highway patrol officer), it doesn't really fit thematically for most Werewolf games (imo).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T13:02:47-07:00","id":944477,"title":"","content":"-Not everything that pings wyrm is of the wyrm<br /> -Vampires beat kinfolk<br /> -That kinfolk will just be a nuisance to higher powers, with all their stoppages. <br /> <br /> Also the kind of kinfolk who get gifts are the ones who don't need sense wyrm to know what's wyrm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7244-innocent-flower","name":"Innocent Flower","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7244_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T13:18:07-07:00","id":944491,"title":"","content":"Thought for a while that a Wyrm detecting Talen would be good for Kinfolk.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T13:28:39-07:00","id":944499,"title":"","content":"Well, Kinfolk with Numina would be much more likely. Anyway, Kinfolk do not have to do anything more than observe and report. If the highway patrol officer was Kinfolk, he can keep an eye out for suspicious activity and send a report to his kin. In addition, it is someone the Garou can call when they need official help. It is sometimes better to let mortals handle things like fomori and ghouls while the Garou deal with the main threat. Of course, vampires can play the same game in the cities with their ghouls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T14:34:22-07:00","id":944520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/943754-police-in-wod?p=944499#post944499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Well, Kinfolk with Numina would be much more likely. Anyway, Kinfolk do not have to do anything more than observe and report. If the highway patrol officer was Kinfolk, he can keep an eye out for suspicious activity and send a report to his kin. In addition, it is someone the Garou can call when they need official help. It is sometimes better to let mortals handle things like fomori and ghouls while the Garou deal with the main threat. Of course, vampires can play the same game in the cities with their ghouls.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know why you are think kinfolk with numina idea should be a regular thing, but I suppose that's neither here nor there. I do agree that if a kinfolk sees something they should pass the information along and not be personally involved.<br /> From a Garou point of view, kinfolk have no business being anywhere around confronting Fomori. And almost certainly not ghouls either. There are exceptions I know, but exceptions are specifically that. Kinfolk are regular-ish people, only slightly better informed (sometimes) and that's about it. Fomori will generally slaughter them. And ghouls have several advantages over kinfolk, even if they are more minor ones (compared to fomori). No Garou should want or allow their family to get involved in life and death fights.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T14:55:19-07:00","id":944537,"title":"","content":"Oh, I am not talking about the Kinfolk attacking them, I am talking about the mortals who the Kinfolk work with attacking them. The Garou just tell the Kinfolk what to report and the Kinfolk let SWAT handle things (or whatever equivalent special response force exists it the area).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T15:44:40-07:00","id":944573,"title":"","content":"Presumably, the people who would be working with a kinfolk officers are their friends and coworkers whom they also wouldn't want to see killed horribly. I suppose I could see police going after ghouls since they are generally more human, but they shouldn't be sent anywhere near fomori on purpose.<br /> Admittedly, the idea of Garou calling in police to handle any sort of problem for them is odd to me. I only see the Garou having contacts in the police dept to tip them off to things, not to actually confront anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T00:29:07-07:00","id":944747,"title":"","content":"To go to the original question; I generally handle the police and other similar agencies as a complication, rather than a regular presence. They're something you have to deal with when something goes wrong, something to avoid, or something that signals it's time to move on. It's very rare when they show up directly in the game, though there have been exceptions.<br /> <br /> One notable exception was when the coterie was trying to find a hunter (not imbued hunter, the more normal kind) who had killed a couple ghouls thinking they were kindred. One of the players went to the crime scene of a recent such murder, posing as a reporter (and making judicious use of Dominate to make the ruse work) and started asking the lead detective some questions. He noticed the detective refused to make eye-contact and started getting curious. He subsequently became very interested in this detective and would make frequent visits with the detective.<br /> <br /> He eventually learned the detective was well aware of the kindred presence in the city, and that he wasn't alone. Most of the police force either had figured out that there were real monsters out there or they had some degree of suspicion that not everything they saw could be explained. Nobody talked about it, but everyone knew. And they knew enough to not want to know more. So when a dead body was found mysteriously drained of all blood, maybe the coroner called it a heart-attack, or exposure to the elements, or a drug overdose. But nobody is going to risk their job by writing down &quot;vampire attack&quot;. Maybe that really was a pack of wild dogs running through Starbucks, but nobody's going to report a werewolf sighting. Sometimes they have to get more creative when explaining away the strange things they see, but there's always some rational explanation in the report. Because the truth would just be too frightening.<br /> <br /> The group grew to love this detective and the perspective he gave on their world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writing up Clanbook: Aabbt","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/700-vysha","name":"Vysha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar700_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"602"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T07:10:08-07:00","id":944825,"title":"","content":"One of my favorite ploys is to have the FBI snooping around after my players do something stupid. A couple of sessions of dodging Special Agents generally gives them a reason to be discrete later on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T16:04:50-07:00","id":945117,"title":"","content":"Here's a line I'm going to put in my game from Malcolm (Vampire 2nd Edition):<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Cops? The first thing you need to know about cops as a vampire is they're superstitious. Cops don't believe in vampires. They don't believe in werewolves, fairies (unless they're making a insult), or goat-suckers. They kind of believe in ghosts but even then, they shrug it off when people claim there's one in the hall.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;However, cops are aware there's stuff which is WEIRD out there. They'll believe in all of the shit I just mentioned if it's right in front of them. They'll shoot at it. Call in backup. Run like Hell. Maybe even use the fire grenades no cop is supposed to have but plenty do. Then, afterward, they'll say it was tweakers, PCP, bath salts, body armor, or some voodoo gang with an accent on the racism. They'll even force themselves to forget--all without the use of Dominate&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;That's how cops work and how they've worked since the Dark Ages. Why? Because if monsters are real, then it's their job to take care of them and no one wants that responsibility.&quot;</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 08-06-2016, 09:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T14:47:55-07:00","id":946475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/943754-police-in-wod?p=944825#post944825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of my favorite ploys is to have the FBI snooping around after my players do something stupid. A couple of sessions of dodging Special Agents generally gives them a reason to be discrete later on.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have also done that before. Especially after a group of PC's used explosives to blow UP a Sabbat's haven...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T14:58:59-07:00","id":946486,"title":"","content":"Ouch. You need the ATF too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T15:24:36-07:00","id":948899,"title":"","content":"Oh, how quickly do you think a changeling could win a newly enchanted police officer over to her side?<br /> <br /> to get him to help her rather then thinking &quot;they've drugged me!!!!!&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> or an important question is how inherently Banal is police work?<br /> <br /> Theirs changelings working as school teachers.<br /> <br /> and oh on Wraiths, on one hand, police protect Life, on the other hand they often deal with Death<br /> <br /> Ideas of a good Shroud rating around a police station.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T20:20:18-07:00","id":952240,"title":"","content":"oh curious What can supernaturals do, when kinfolk, ghouls, Mediums, bystanders, Kinain, what have you, are in jail.<br /> <br /> assuming their valued enough not to be casually dismissed as irrelevant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T20:26:59-07:00","id":952248,"title":"","content":"It depends on the supernatural. A Ventrue with Dominate and Presence could just talk their ghoul out of prison.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T20:34:23-07:00","id":952252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/943754-police-in-wod?p=952248#post952248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It depends on the supernatural. A Ventrue with Dominate and Presence could just talk their ghoul out of prison.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not a masquerade breach at all. Nope, no sir.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T21:09:18-07:00","id":952268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/943754-police-in-wod?p=952252#post952252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's not a masquerade breach at all. Nope, no sir.</div> </div> </div> </div>As the old adage goes, it's not a Masquerade breach if nobody talks about it!<br /> <br /> Ahem. More seriously though, going after the judge at night is a better alternative. Sneak into (or get invited to) his house, use your mind-whammy on him in private, then have him throw the case out on some technicality your well-paid-for lawyer brings up. It'll attract far less attention than why a prisoner who the records state should be in lock-up suddenly isn't. And the ghoul gets to sweat it out in lock-up for a few nights to a few weeks. A suitable punishment for such sloppy work. You should expect better from such a trusted servant!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writing up Clanbook: Aabbt","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/700-vysha","name":"Vysha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar700_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"602"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T21:25:09-07:00","id":952278,"title":"","content":"Seems more in line with Vampire for the Ventrue to use influences to get this sort of thing done. Why get personally involved at all if you don't have to.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/943754-police-in-wod?p=952240#post952240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">oh curious What can supernaturals do, when kinfolk, ghouls, Mediums, bystanders, Kinain, what have you, are in jail.<br /> <br /> assuming their valued enough not to be casually dismissed as irrelevant.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, just my 2 cents:<br /> For all of the Supernatural types, I think it really would depend on circumstance. What did the kinfolk/ghoul/etc actually do to get themselves locked up and how long will they be gone? If I found out my sibling (thinking kinfolk now) killed their spouse for example, they might deserve to rot. I would look into it, but if everything seems aboveboard and I think they did it, then that's that.<br /> <br /> If this was some sort of set as payback and the kinfolk/ghoul/etc is being put away then it becomes another matter.<br /> Vampires have influences or can call in the people that do for boons, so I do think that's the way it would be handled. Less favored kindred might resort to a heavy handed approach where they Discipline their way out of the situation, but that is going to lead to issues really quick.<br /> <br /> For Garou....I have to imagine that there are kinfolk gangs in jail and that they look out for their own. So they would be on their best behavior and you'll see them when they get out. If the kinfolk is really valued and relative to a younger (read: Rank 0-1) Garou, I could see them doing something stupid enough to get the FBI involved (this has happened in a game before for me).<br /> <br /> Changelings can really do anything that Vampires can in regards to the heavy handed approach. Influences, usually less so.<br /> <br /> Mediums....I think it really depends on what friends you have on the other side. It could be a fairly easy task to alter computer logs and have someone let go. And if it was a setup, I would certainly be concerned having an angry Wraith (hopefully) against me.<br /> <br /> Bystanders are shit out of luck. Hell, most hunters are as well.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T05:09:05-07:00","id":952434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/943754-police-in-wod?p=952252#post952252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's not a masquerade breach at all. Nope, no sir.</div> </div> </div> </div>It might be from a <i>prison</i><br /> <br /> <br /> but from county jail, when a suspects guilt hasnt been proven yet?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T06:48:11-07:00","id":952477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/943754-police-in-wod?p=952434#post952434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It might be from a <i>prison</i><br /> <br /> <br /> but from county jail, when a suspects guilt hasnt been proven yet?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sheriff: Deputy why did you release that man? He never posted bail.<br /> Deputy: Well this guy came in and he was really nice and you know I really wanted to help him out. I don't quite remember his face but he was really nice and now that I think about it my head hurts......","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T07:12:29-07:00","id":952490,"title":"","content":"I think a Ventrue can probably post bail. Anyway, if a Ventrue is willing to let their ghoul go to prison, as opposed to jail, they probably have abandoned them to their fate because they have already been tried and convicted (in the USA, prison is supposed to be only for convicted criminals while jail is supposed to be only for suspected criminals, though some jails do hold minor level convicted criminals).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T07:22:52-07:00","id":952498,"title":"","content":"I usually run them as rather corrupt, with some very corrupt elements and more than in real life, and a rare few gems of honest people.<br /> <br /> And as a mention, I don't pretend that this is how the police is in real life but rather a much darker mirror image of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T07:51:29-07:00","id":952512,"title":"","content":"my mom and sister have both been screwed over by speedtraps a time or two.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com